{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Now he brings proof for his words." "<b>The meaning of כליותי</b> — they are the hidden places, and they are the internal organs, for they are in the inner abdomen. Some say: the kidneys are created first, for they are like the two bearings of the sphere. Some say: because they have power over the desire for intercourse, therefore they are called כליות from the root of: נכספה וגם כלתה נפשי (Job 14:22 — my soul longs and pines)." "<b>תסכני</b> — although it has a samekh, it is like ובעצמות וגידים תסוככני (Job 10:11). And behold the meaning: for You acquired me and screened me in my mother's womb, which is hidden and there is no light there."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {1 "The verse cited is Job 14:22; resolved based on the root argument about desire/longing.", 2 "The comparison is to Job 10:11, where תסוככני uses sin rather than samekh, supporting his point about the root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:13.687045545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}